    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Santiago DeSoto Embraced Miguel Santo Domingo, a small-time bandit, in 1920s Brazil, recognizing a kindred buccaneer spirit. Miguel became pack priest of the nomadic Navigators &mdash; a floating pack that raids @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.fc464242d84d4e34]{Camarilla} enclaves along the Great Lakes and Saint Lawrence Seaway from their lair-ship, the <em>Lisbon</em> &mdash; when DeSoto joined the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat} Inquisition in 1969. DeSoto's abrupt retirement into seclusion after the trial of Archbishop Sangris has only deepened Miguel's suspicion that his sire hides some dark secret; in truth, &quot;DeSoto&quot; is now the resting place of Sangris' own soul, and Miguel is unknowingly correct.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Direct and straightforward, devious only when necessary, open among your pack and friends. You ride your frenzy with pleasure when destroying the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat}'s enemies.</p>",
    "notes": "Embraced 1924. Apparent age: early 30s. @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.paths-of-enlightenment.JournalEntry.MkHKLOcOCLQ5pWCj]{Path of Honorable Accord} 8. Disciplines (as printed): Celerity 3, Fortitude 2, Potence 4, Presence 3.",
